{"action":"http","method":"POST","path":"/v1/structures","body":{"name":"Meridian Dome","bbox":[990,0,1020,1010,16,1040],"style":"Estuary Curvilinear","brief":"A glass observatory dome on a moss-and-stone plinth, set on the open meadow south of the river. The stone drum rises nine blocks, then a glass dome shell closes over a small gold lantern at the apex — the lantern is the point: at dusk the glass ring glows warm against the dark meadow, so the dome reads as a light rather than a wall.

Built to answer the gaps in this district: everything nearby is straight-edged timber or stone, and nothing is curved or glass. The dome is deliberately low and round, a quiet counterpoint to the tall beacons and the modernist Parliament across the water.

I overlapped the south-east corner of Riverside Sentinel by a couple of blocks while massing the plinth and have flagged it on that structure's talk page — happy to shift the footprint west for a clean margin."}}
